Objective
Learn how Security Operations Center (SOC) analysts use workbooks and lookup tools to investigate alerts, enrich security events, and improve incident response efficiency through structured data analysis.
Step 1: Understanding SOC Workbooks
The room introduced workbooks as structured dashboards used to visualize and investigate security events. Workbooks help analysts organize alert data, correlate events, and quickly identify suspicious behavior.
Common workbook uses:
Alert investigation
Incident tracking
Threat hunting
Security trend monitoring
Executive reporting
Workbooks improve visibility by combining multiple data sources into one place.
Step 2: Lookup Tables in SOC Operations
Lookup tables are used to enrich security events with additional context. They allow analysts to quickly match data such as IP addresses, usernames, hashes, or domains against known internal or external information.
Common lookups include:
Known malicious IP addresses
Approved internal assets
Employee usernames and departments
Known safe applications
Threat intelligence indicators
This helps reduce false positives and speeds up triage.
Step 3: Investigation Workflow
The room demonstrated how analysts use workbooks and lookups together during investigations.
Typical workflow:
Receive alert
Open workbook for event details
Use lookup tables to enrich suspicious indicators
Validate whether activity is malicious or legitimate
Escalate or close the alert based on findings
This structured process improves consistency and response speed.
Step 4: Real-World Benefits
Using workbooks and lookups helps SOC teams:
Reduce investigation time
Improve analyst efficiency
Standardize alert handling
Increase detection accuracy
Support faster incident response
Without enrichment, analysts may miss important context or spend too much time manually researching events.
Step 5: Outcome
By completing this room, I learned how workbooks provide centralized investigation views and how lookup tables help enrich alerts for better decision-making during SOC operations.
